From: frogro <frogro@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] apple: select USB4 or TB3 EFI boot from negotiated cable mode

Integrate the native USB4 v1 single-hop router configuration, discovered
PCIe adapters, buffer queries, validated HopID paths and read-only NVMe
EFI boot. Preserve vendor-defined protocol-adapter flow-control fields.

Use mutually exclusive TB3 and USB4 dispatch, independent of diagnostic
stage flags. Leave internal/USB bootflow available without a supported
external link. Preserve normal U-Boot entry, EFI handover and reset on a
returning modified-controller path. No forced diagnostic main loop, disk
log writes, fixed external filesystem UUID or m1n1 changes are included.

Current pre-OS scope remains J274 port1, one external router and one NVMe
namespace. USB4 v2, downstream dock chains and port0 are not validated.

